 138:/Users/timcarlo/Desktop/testsoftware/common/utils/machester.c **** /*
 139:/Users/timcarlo/Desktop/testsoftware/common/utils/machester.c **** The 433.92 Mhz receivers have AGC, if no signal is present the gain will be set
 140:/Users/timcarlo/Desktop/testsoftware/common/utils/machester.c **** to its highest level.
 141:/Users/timcarlo/Desktop/testsoftware/common/utils/machester.c **** 
 142:/Users/timcarlo/Desktop/testsoftware/common/utils/machester.c **** In this condition it will switch high to low at random intervals due to input noise.
 143:/Users/timcarlo/Desktop/testsoftware/common/utils/machester.c **** A CRO connected to the data line looks like 433.92 is full of transmissions.
 144:/Users/timcarlo/Desktop/testsoftware/common/utils/machester.c **** 
 145:/Users/timcarlo/Desktop/testsoftware/common/utils/machester.c **** Any ASK transmission method must first sent a capture signal of 101010........
 146:/Users/timcarlo/Desktop/testsoftware/common/utils/machester.c **** When the receiver has adjusted its AGC to the required level for the transmisssion
 147:/Users/timcarlo/Desktop/testsoftware/common/utils/machester.c **** the actual data transmission can occur.
 148:/Users/timcarlo/Desktop/testsoftware/common/utils/machester.c **** 
 149:/Users/timcarlo/Desktop/testsoftware/common/utils/machester.c **** We send 14 0's 1010... It takes 1 to 3 10's for the receiver to adjust to
 150:/Users/timcarlo/Desktop/testsoftware/common/utils/machester.c **** the transmit level.
 151:/Users/timcarlo/Desktop/testsoftware/common/utils/machester.c **** 
 152:/Users/timcarlo/Desktop/testsoftware/common/utils/machester.c **** The receiver waits until we have at least 10 10's and then a start pulse 01.
 153:/Users/timcarlo/Desktop/testsoftware/common/utils/machester.c **** The receiver is then operating correctly and we have locked onto the transmission.
 154:/Users/timcarlo/Desktop/testsoftware/common/utils/machester.c **** */
